hermes v0.23.0 (+ the vault-payment and isolated-world patches): a saved
payment card (and an address) fills only on the exact origin it was saved
for (`_bound_page_origin`, `snapshot_refusal`); a card saved without an
origin never fills. One card is used on many shops, so the agent asked for
the same card again per site, or proposed workarounds around the vault.

Dave's rule (hyperhermes): a saved card or address fills on ANY website,
and every fill needs the user's explicit confirmation naming the exact
page origin (and the processor frame origins for hosted card fields, and
the total the page shows, best effort and marked unverified). Logins and
their one-time codes stay bound to their exact saved origins: that binding
is the phishing guard.

Change:
- tools/browser_vault_context.py `fills_on_any_site(meta)`: payment and
  address. `snapshot_refusal` accepts such an item if the re-read item is
  still the same kind.
- `_bound_page_origin`: for those kinds, the one open tab holding a form
  of this kind (`focus_page(unique=True)` probes every tab; several such
  tabs are refused as `ambiguous_page`, since the tool can't tell which one
  the agent drives), else the current page (a saved origin is only a hint
  and never picks a tab); only http(s) pages, and https for cards (plain
  http only on loopback, parsed with urlsplit + ipaddress); returns that
  page's origin.
- `browser_vault_fill`: addresses get the confirmation too (previously
  cards only). The prompt (`_confirm_payment_fill`) names the page origin,
  the saved-for origin when it differs ("this page is a different site"),
  the processor frame origins and a page-shown total reduced to a currency
  mark and digits (description only, marked unverified). The title leads
  with the site (a long host cut from the left, so its real end shows) and
  ends with the agent-chosen label and a per-fill tag, so the gateway
  never merges two fills' prompts into one answer. No remember_key: every
  fill asks once, nothing carries to the next fill or to another origin;
  decline, cancel, timeout and headless sessions write nothing.
- `enter_code` takes only a login's handle (a card handle is refused).
- The confirmed origin is the one the two-phase write pins (value-free
  precheck and the in-script `expectedOrigin` assert, in the isolated
  world); the frame-ancestry checks still require processor frames embedded
  directly by that page. Unchanged for logins.
- `browser_vault action=list`: cards and addresses are `available` with
  `sites: "any site; the user confirms each fill"`; no values.
- `hermes vault add` asks for an optional hint origin for cards/addresses.

Tests: tests/tools/test_browser_vault_payment_consent.py (unseen site
fills only after consent naming it, declined/cancel writes nothing, asked
on every fill, no remember_key, card without origin, amount, non-web page
refused), test_browser_vault_origin_guard.py (login/code still refused on
another origin; card/address declined = nothing resolved; accepted =
write pinned to the confirmed origin), test_vault_payment_iframe.py
(snapshot must stay a card).

Residual: `delegation.subagent_auto_approve: true` (not set by
hyperhermes) answers a subagent's prompts "once", which would confirm a
card fill without the user. The desktop app's vault settings still ask an
origin for cards (cosmetic).

Not upstream; carried by hyperhermes as Dave's policy.

